---
import FlagshipLayout from "../../layouts/FlagshipLayout.astro";
import FlagshipBreadcrumbs from "../../components/FlagshipBreadcrumbs.astro";
import { currentProgram as program } from "../../data/currentProgram";
---

<FlagshipLayout
  title="Young Competition Speakers · Fall 2026 | SpeakKai"
  description="An 18-class public speaking course for Grades 1–2. Explore the practice cycle, speaking roles, feedback and a free sample activity."
  contactHref="/contact/?audience=coaching"
  breadcrumb="Young Competition Speakers"
>
  <section class="wrap course-intro">
    <FlagshipBreadcrumbs label={program.name} />
    <p class="eyebrow">{program.season} · {program.audience}</p>
    <h1>Small speaking moments.<br /><em>A voice of their own.</em></h1>
    <p class="course-name">{program.name}</p>
    <p class="hero-lead">
      Turn current topics, stories and real-world roles into short, achievable
      speaking challenges.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/contact/?audience=coaching"
        >Ask about the course <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      ><a class="text-link" href="/resources/one-object-story/"
        >Try a free practice activity <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <dl class="course-facts">
      <div><dt>Course</dt><dd>18 classes</dd></div><div>
        <dt>Structure</dt><dd>6 × 3-class units</dd>
      </div><div><dt>Practice speeches</dt><dd>60–90 seconds</dd></div><div>
        <dt>Final showcase</dt><dd>Supported · 3 minutes</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section class="practice-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">A repeatable learning cycle</p><h2>
          Explore. Build. Present.
        </h2><p>
          Each three-class unit follows this sequence. Every class begins with
          articulation, body and voice warm-ups.
        </p>
      </div><ol class="method-grid">
        {
          program.sequence.map((step, index) => (
            <li>
              <>
                <span class="index">0{index + 1}</span>
                <h3>{step.title}</h3>
                <p>{step.detail}</p>
              </>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section course-worlds">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Ideas worth talking about</p><h2>
        Real questions.<br />Different points of view.
      </h2><p>
        Speaking has a purpose when there is something interesting to think
        about.
      </p><ul>{program.themes.map((theme) => <li>{theme}</li>)}</ul>
    </div><div>
      <h3>Try a speaker’s role</h3><p>
        A role gives the learner an audience and a reason to speak.
      </p><ul class="role-list">
        {program.roles.map((role) => <li>{role}</li>)}
      </ul><p class="section-note">
        Themes and roles describe the course’s range. Their order and specific
        class activities are shaped for the group.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="practice-section">
    <div class="wrap feedback-example">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What useful feedback sounds like</p><h2>
          Notice a choice.<br /><em>Try one change.</em>
        </h2><p>
          This illustrative exchange shows how feedback can point to a next
          action.
        </p>
      </div><div class="feedback-card">
        <p class="example-label">
          Example feedback · not a student testimonial
        </p><p>
          “Your example helped me picture the scene. Try pausing before your
          last sentence so I can hear why it matters.”
        </p><p class="field-note">
          The learner tries the ending again. The listener notices what changed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section course-decide">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you decide</p><h2>
        Bring the learner’s<br />starting point.
      </h2><p>
        Share their grade, speaking experience and any event they are preparing
        for. Kai can discuss whether this course or another coaching format is a
        suitable fit.
      </p><p>
        Exact dates, class length, location or online format, fees and
        availability are confirmed with Kai. The course does not guarantee
        competition results.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/contact/?audience=coaching"
          >Prepare a parent inquiry <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        ><a class="text-link" href="/coaching/">All student coaching</a>
      </div>
    </div><aside>
      <h3>Start with one object.</h3><p>
        A familiar object can become a short story. Try the free 10-minute
        starter with a listener at home.
      </p><a class="text-link" href="/resources/one-object-story/"
        >Open the practice sheet <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      ><p class="section-note">
        An example activity to try, rather than a complete class or placement
        assessment.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>
</FlagshipLayout>
<style>
  .course-intro {
    padding-block: 36px 60px;
  }
  .course-intro > .eyebrow {
    margin-top: 32px;
    color: var(--blue);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.1vw, 70px);
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .course-name {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .hero-lead {
    max-width: 670px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .course-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 22px;
    margin: 44px 0 0;
    padding-top: 26px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  dt {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .course-worlds,
  .feedback-example,
  .course-decide {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 70px;
  }
  .course-worlds h2,
  .feedback-example h2,
  .course-decide h2 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 3.3vw, 46px);
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .course-worlds p,
  .feedback-example p,
  .course-decide p {
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .course-worlds h3,
  .course-decide h3 {
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .course-worlds ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .role-list {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  }
  .feedback-card {
    padding: 30px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--yellow);
    background: white;
  }
  .feedback-card .example-label {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .feedback-card > p:nth-child(2) {
    font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .feedback-card .field-note {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .course-decide aside {
    background: var(--wash);
    padding: 30px;
    align-self: start;
  }
  .course-decide aside .text-link {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .course-facts {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 24px 16px;
    }
    dd {
      font-size: 18px;
    }
    .course-worlds,
    .feedback-example,
    .course-decide {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 34px;
    }
    .role-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
    .course-intro {
      padding-top: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
